            "review_title": "Review at NOA Dining & Club",
            "review_text": "наталья п\n2 contributions\n0\nHow time was wasted, ruined the taste in your mouth, mood, and you even had to pay money.\nSep 2026 • Couples\nWe just wanted to eat ice cream and go on. The pleasant interior caught my attention, so we came here. The ice cream in the menu was the only coconut one for 180,000 dong, we ordered it. Waited for 15 minutes, already regretted coming here. They still brought it, and it turned out to have an \"original presentation\"—the coconut ball was in a coconut cup, which contained some foam in addition to the ice cream. This foam tasted very disgusting and salty ((I wanted to spit it out, but I held back. I think I'll move this ball into the cup. I took out a coconut, put a ball in the dish, the light was dim, it seemed like coconut flakes were poured into the cup, but it turned out to be salt!!! In the end, after breaking off a piece of ice cream, hoping to eat away that nasty foam, she ate a spoonful of salt in the coconut ice cream. In the end, she ran to the toilet to rinse her mouth. They still made me pay for the ice cream, even though they explained that ice cream is supposed to be sweet, not salty foam and salt((( in the end, I wasted time, ruined my taste and mood, and had to pay money too. I do not recommend it.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten September 27, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
